A good read
1 Read the information. Discuss the questions in pairs or small groups.
There are two forms of writing: fiction and non-fiction.
Fiction is writing about imaginary people and events. It includes short stories and long
stories (called novels), poems and plays.
Non-fiction is writing about real people, events and things. It gives information with facts.
It includes newspaper articles, school textbooks, cookery books and travel writing.
▸
▸
