2 Different types of fiction are called genres.
Read these descriptions of some popular
genres and choose your three favourite.
Genre
Features
adventure
Involves a lot of action, often fights (sometimes wars), chases, crashes and
plenty of bravery and excitement.
humour
Strange characters doing funny things to cause laughter and entertainment.
traditional
Stories that were passed down orally, including folktales, fairy tales and
fables from different cultures.
crime / mystery
Involves a crime or mystery. The reader tries to solve the mystery at the
same time as the lead character.
science fiction
Set in the future using science and technology (e.g. robots, spaceships or
time travel).
fantasy
A story in an imaginary world with strange settings and characters, often
includes amazing creatures.
historical fiction
Fictional stories set in history, bringing famous people and places to life.
